      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ultra-low bitrate encoding is an interesting use case. There are real life scenarios where libaom @ CQ 63 might result in too big of a file, while other video standards can still go much lower.\n\nPrior art: SVT-AV1 4.0 implements its own CRF extension (from 63 to 70), where CRF 70 files are roughly half the size of their CRF 63 counterparts: https://gitlab.com/AOMediaCodec/SVT-AV1/-/merge_requests/2522. This feature has come in handy a few times.\n\nThat said: libaom implements frame scaling, so maybe leveraging this feature is the most straightforward to bridge the bitrate gap for the AV1 vs. AV2 subjective test.",
      "parentUuid": "2c989d17_480cf812",
